    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-UpdateAddOnMemoryUsage-15",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "UpdateAddOnMemoryUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - UpdateAddOnMemoryUsage() - Scan through memory profiling data and update the per-addon statistics",
      "wikitext_line": 15,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetAddOnMemoryUsage-16",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetAddOnMemoryUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - usedKB = GetAddOnMemoryUsage(index or \"name\") - query an addon's memory use (in K, precision to 1 byte) - This returns a cached value calculated by UpdateAddOnMemoryUsage().",
      "wikitext_line": 16,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-cvars-scriptProfile-19",
      "section": "cvars",
      "direction": "changed",
      "symbol": "scriptProfile",
      "annotation": "* CPU profiling is disabled by default since it has some overhead. CPU profiling is controlled by the scriptProfile cvar, which persists across sessions, and takes effect after a UI reload.",
      "wikitext_line": 19,
      "kind": "prose-cvar",
      "publication_boundary": "literal-contract-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetScriptCPUUsage-21",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetScriptCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - time = GetScriptCPUUsage() - Returns the total timeused by the scripting system",
      "wikitext_line": 21,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-UpdateAddOnCPUUsage-22",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "UpdateAddOnCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - UpdateAddOnCPUUsage() - Scan through the profiling data and update the per-addon statistics",
      "wikitext_line": 22,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetAddOnCPUUsage-23",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetAddOnCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - time = GetAddOnCPUUsage(index or \\\"name\\\") - Returns the total time used by the specified AddOn. This returns a cached value calculated by UpdateAddOnCPUUsage().",
      "wikitext_line": 23,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetFunctionCPUUsage-24",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetFunctionCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - time, count = GetFunctionCPUUsage(function[, includeSubroutines]) - Returns the time used and number of times the specified function was called. If 'includeSubroutines' is true or omitted, the time includes both the time spent in the function and subroutines called by the function. If it is false, then time is only the time actually spent by the code in the function itself.",
      "wikitext_line": 24,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetFrameCPUUsage-25",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetFrameCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - time, count = GetFrameCPUUsage(frame[, includeChildren]) - Returns the time used and number of function calls of any of the frame's script handlers. If 'includeChildren' is true or omitted, the time and call count will include the handlers for all of the frame's children as well.",
      "wikitext_line": 25,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-GetEventCPUUsage-26",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "GetEventCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - time, count = GetEventCPUUsage([\"event\"]) - Returns the time used and number of times the specified event has been triggered. If 'event' is omitted, the time and count will be totals across all events.",
      "wikitext_line": 26,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-global-api-ResetCPUUsage-27",
      "section": "global-api",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "ResetCPUUsage",
      "annotation": "* NEW - ResetCPUUsage() - Reset all CPU profiling statistics to zero. ",
      "wikitext_line": 27,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-widgets-Frame:HookScript-32",
      "section": "widgets",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "Frame:HookScript",
      "annotation": "* NEW - Frame:HookScript(\"name\", function) - Exactly equivalent to hooksecurefunc(), but usable with frame script handlers. (Note that like hooksecurefunc(), this is not intended as a general hooking replacement, but to allow hooking of secure frame handlers.)",
      "wikitext_line": 32,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
    {
      "id": "wt-widgets-Frame:GetEffectiveAlpha-33",
      "section": "widgets",
      "direction": "added",
      "symbol": "Frame:GetEffectiveAlpha",
      "annotation": "* NEW - alpha = Frame:GetEffectiveAlpha() - Returns the effective alpha of a frame, which is logically Frame:GetParent():GetEffectiveAlpha() * Frame:GetAlpha()",
      "wikitext_line": 33,
      "kind": "labeled-call",
      "publication_boundary": "source-claim-only"
    },
